WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:04.357
Hey Traveler! Team Lab shows what each
teammate really brings with honest numbers

2
00:00:04.407 --> 00:00:05.219
and clear labels.

3
00:00:07.700 --> 00:00:09.322
Let's Start with four empty slots.

4
00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:13.651
Turn on Use my characters
to see only who you own.

5
00:00:16.233 --> 00:00:20.926
I'll pick Xiangling, Bennett, Kazooha and
Furina for Vaporize. Each uses my saved

6
00:00:20.976 --> 00:00:24.264
build, and gaps are filled
from a labelled Guide Example.

7
00:00:25.867 --> 00:00:30.325
Each teammate's buffs are either Calculated,
with a number when switched on, or

8
00:00:30.375 --> 00:00:32.550
Described: real, just not a number yet.

9
00:00:34.367 --> 00:00:38.638
Team Lab also reads roles and reactions,
like Vaporize and Swirl, labelled as a

10
00:00:38.688 --> 00:00:39.239
suggestion.

11
00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:44.450
What your teammates add compares each
character's biggest hits, alone and with the

12
00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:45.176
buffs you choose.

13
00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:52.010
I'll switch on Bennett's Burst and Kazuha's
Pyro Swirl buff. Only pick buffs you'd

14
00:00:52.060 --> 00:00:53.198
really have up together.

15
00:00:55.767 --> 00:01:00.166
Xiangling's hits jump. These are single-hit
estimates under those conditions, not

16
00:01:00.216 --> 00:01:00.825
team damage.

17
00:01:02.033 --> 00:01:04.955
Add a reaction share, and keep
that assumption realistic.

18
00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:10.910
To compare pin Setup A and change one
thing, like Kazuha at constellation two.

19
00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:14.709
You'll see what changed, what's
verified, and what stays unknown.

20
00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:20.297
Each teammate's full list shows what isn't
modelled yet, like parts of Furina's kit.

21
00:01:22.667 --> 00:01:27.549
Remember: single-hit comparisons, not
team DPS. Uptimes, swaps and energy aren't

22
00:01:27.599 --> 00:01:29.768
simulated, so real rotations differ.

23
00:01:30.633 --> 00:01:33.648
Happy with it? Save the team,
or download a share card.

24
00:01:35.767 --> 00:01:38.550
Build the team that's fun
for you. See you next time!
